# <%= name %>

A <%= spa ? "client-only" : "server-rendered" %> Svelte application built on Canonical's design system and
`@canonical/styles`, with SvelteKit for routing, loading<% if (!spa) { %>, form actions and
streaming<% } %>.

Use `summon domain billing --framework svelte`, `summon page billing/detail
--framework svelte` and `summon wrapper settings --framework svelte` to add
SvelteKit routes and wrappers.

## Quick start

```sh
bun install
bun run dev
```

Commit the lockfile and install with `bun install --frozen-lockfile` in CI.

## Builds

| Build | Command | Output | Serve |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
<% if (spa) { -%>
| SPA (adapter-static) | `bun run build` | `build/` | any static host, with `200.html` as the fallback for every app route |
<% } else { -%>
| SSR (adapter-node) | `bun run build` | `build/` | `bun run preview` (`node build/index.js`; Bun runs it too) |
<% } -%>
| Storybook | `bun run build:storybook` | `storybook-static/` | any static host |

<% if (spa) { -%>
Every route renders in the browser: the theme<% if (intl) { %> and locale<% } %> come from <% if (intl) { %>their cookies
and the browser's languages<% } else { %>its cookie<% } %>, and the forms have no server to post to. A cold
request gets no route-specific HTTP status and no server-rendered content.
<% } else { -%>
Set `HOST`, `PORT` and `ORIGIN` for the SSR build as adapter-node documents.
<% } -%>

## Testing

```sh
bun run test:unit     # Vitest, the pure modules, in Node
bun run test:browser  # builds, then Playwright Chromium against the <%= spa ? "static build" : "SSR server" %>
bun run test          # both
```

The browser tests need Playwright's Chromium (`bunx playwright install
chromium`); set `CHROMIUM_PATH` to use another executable<% if (!spa) { %>, and
`SERVER_RUNTIME=bun` to run the SSR build with Bun<% } %>.

