### Page layouts

Layouts are route groups, so a page never renders its own frame. Every page
except the 404 sits under `(top-bar)`: a top bar with the app's name, one link
per area of the scaffold, and the theme<% if (intl) { %> and language<% } %> selector<% if (intl) { %>s<% } %>. The links are demo
navigation for exploring what the scaffold ships — replace them with your own.
<% if (appShell) { -%>
Under the top bar a page takes one of two layouts:

- `(public)` — the public pages: one constrained column.
- `dashboard` — `ApplicationShell` from `src/lib`: the design system's
  `ApplicationLayout` with its `SideNavigation`. Each dashboard page renders
  `ViewLayout` and `ContentLayout` inside it.

The dashboard's navigation is one tree of navigation items, built in
`src/domains/dashboard/createDashboardNavigation.ts`. The side navigation
renders it, and the breadcrumbs are projected from it.
<% } else { -%>
The public pages render under it in `(public)`, one constrained column.
<% } -%>

## Theme<% if (intl) { %> and language<% } %>

<% if (intl) { -%>
With JavaScript, the theme and language selectors apply on change: `setTheme`
swaps the theme class on `<html>` and writes the `theme` cookie, and the locale
source re-translates the page, flips `<html lang dir>` and writes the `locale`
cookie.
<% } else { -%>
With JavaScript, the theme selector applies on change: `setTheme` swaps the
theme class on `<html>` and writes the `theme` cookie.
<% } -%>
<% if (spa) { -%>
The client-only build reads the cookie<% if (intl) { %>s<% } %> back on every load.
<% } else { -%>
Without JavaScript, each selector is a form that posts to `/preferences`<% if (intl) { %> or
`/language`<% } %>, which sets the same cookie and sends the reader back; the server then
renders the class<% if (intl) { %>, `lang` and `dir`<% } %>. The Apply buttons sit in `<noscript>`, so
they never show while JavaScript runs.

The cookies are `path=/`, `SameSite=Lax`, a one-year max age, `Secure` over
HTTPS on the server, and not `httpOnly`, so the page can overwrite what the
server set.
<% } -%>
